  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 225 AM EDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nTypical summertime convection pattern with triple digit heat index \nvalues returning this weekend. Conditions are expected to flirt with \nheat advisory criteria at the beginning of next work week. \nEspecially the SE part of the CWA. \n\nFortunately, thunderstorms will be expected each afternoon which may \nhelp ease temperatures during peak heating. There is pretty good \nagreement that afternoon convection will form everyday for the \nforeseeable future, though no strong signal for severe weather \nexists with the limited shear in place. Strength of storms will \nultimately depend on heating.",
